ns include raising by **100** or more. Given the prior bet was 200 pre-flop, a proper raise on the flop should be at least double the previous round’s bet if there were action — but since opponent checked, **you can bet any amount ≥100** (as per valid actions listed). A raise of 100 is reasonable for a half-pot or smaller continuation bet.\n\nReason:  \nYou have top pair, best kicker, plus a nut flush draw — very high equity (~60%+ against most ranges). You should bet for value and protection. A moderate raise of 100 keeps worse hands in while charging draws. Opponent’s passivity suggests weakness, so larger bets risk folding out worse. An all-in overbets the situation. Best balance is a **raise of 100**.\n\nAnswer: 100"}
